n conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le18ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Modals for Possibility and Necessity", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use modal verbs to add meaning to other verbs. They come before the dictionary form (Infinitive without \u2018<span class=\"italic\">to</span>') of the main verb. <br/> Modal verbs can add meaning connected with certainty or necessity.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use modals with a variety of verb tenses. You can use them to talk about possible or necessary actions in the present, past or future. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use modals with the Simple Present tense:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I think the restaurant might be more lucrative if it catered to children. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "(Here, the modal <span class=\"italic\">might</span> adds the meaning of <span class=\"strong\">possibility</span>: It is possible that the restaurant will make more money if it catered to children.)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Modals can also be used in the Passive voice:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">The restaurant may be renovated soon.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I had better meet with you in person. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "All the gossip had better be shared!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "My life may be transformed by my plan!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Why does your restaurant have to be converted?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Organizing Points in an Argument", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use words or phrases to organize ideas in a piece of writing. <br/>Discourse markers show how ideas are connected. They usually come at the beginning of a sentence.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Discourse markers can show a <span class=\"strong\">connection </span>to what the writer is saying and what was just written. They can also show what the writer's <span class=\"strong\">opinion </span>is about what is being discussed. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart for some common discourse markers and their meanings:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Discourse Marker\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">However</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">But</span>; Contrast\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Therefore</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Logical consequence\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">In spite of</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Emphasizing a contrast\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">What is more</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adding\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Of course</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Stating it is obvious\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">In fact</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Emphasizing and adding\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "First, more people are taking their kids out to restaurants. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "In fact, a lot of restaurants don't allow children.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "In other words, families are discriminated against. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "However, people who have children understand about kids and they wouldn't object.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "manicure ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "cosmetic treatment of the fingernails", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: What a great idea to have our nails done together! We can chat and get manicures at the same time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le18ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about rules, regulations and decision-making.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "in person", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to see or meet someone in physical presence", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I needed to talk to you and I thought I had better meet with you in person.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le18ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to spur", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to stimulate or initiate ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You've spurred me to make a transition in my life too.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le18ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "lucrative ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something that is profitable or moneymaking", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm going to change the style of the restaurant. I think it might be more lucrative  if it catered to children. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le18ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to cater to", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to provide or supply food or services to a party or restaurant", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I think I will change the style of the restaurant to cater to children. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le18ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "rationale ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the reasons and arguments for doing something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Your rationale for changing the style of the restaurant  has to be explained!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le18ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to convert", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to change or transform something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Why do you want to convert your restaurant?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le18ob09aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to misbehave", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to have a bad behavior", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There is a reason that some people don't like children in a restaurant. For example, sometimes they are really loud and misbehave. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le18ob09aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to discriminate against", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to treat unfairly a certain group of people ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A lot of restaurants don't allow children. In other words, families are discriminated against. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le18ob09aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "consequence ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the result of something that took place earlier", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You'll lose all the customers who don't have kids. Think of the consequences! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le18ob09aud10", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about rules, regulations and decision-making.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I explain my opinion and organize points in an argument.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I express possibility and necessity.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I debate pros and cons.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Make a list of all the pros (advantages) of changing your career or job to something completely different later in life.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Your partner will make a list of the cons (disadvantages) of changing careers.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Using your list, have a debate with your partner about whether it is a good or bad idea to change your career later in life.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Be sure to use language to organize the points in your argument and to encourage agreement.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about rules, regulations and decision making.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can express possibility and necessity. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can explain my opinion and organize points an argument.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Are you good at making decisions or are you usually indecisive?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Have you ever made a decision and then regretted it? Why?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1